 Two fingers decide between scroll and pinch after one of them moves about 1.2 mm: fingers
 moving in opposite directions (apart or together) pinch, fingers moving the same way scroll.
@@ -29,6 +32,14 @@ their midpoint must start within about 6 mm of the edge) and swipe about 9 mm in
 once, then the gesture is ignored until you lift your fingers. Nothing scrolls while the swipe is
 undecided; moving up, down or outwards, or pinching, from the edge scrolls or pinches as usual.
 
+A flick is a quick two finger swipe sideways anywhere outside the edge zones: about 6 mm in
+150 ms, mostly horizontal (less than 2.5 mm up or down, and at most half as much up or down as
+sideways). Fingers right go back, fingers left go forward, like swiping between pages on a Mac
+trackpad. It fires once, then the gesture is ignored until you lift your fingers. To tell a flick
+from a scroll, horizontal scroll waits up to 150 ms after the fingers start moving and then
+catches up, so nothing is lost; vertical scroll and pinch are not delayed. If flicks fire while
+scrolling, raise `DIGITIZER_FLICK_DISTANCE` or lower `DIGITIZER_FLICK_TIMEOUT`.
+
